 "overview": "This file comprises two sequential sets of U.S. Department of State 'List of Papers' (docket and register sheets) for decimal file 894.20 (Military Affairs - Japan), documenting materials catalogued between 1930 and 1940. The first part (pages 1–8) indexes diplomatic despatches, telegrams, and cross-reference sheets covering internal Japanese military-political developments, including factional struggles in the War Ministry, the August 1935 assassination of Major General Tetsuzan Nagata, the February 26, 1936 coup attempt, the enactment and implementation of the National General Mobilization Law, the establishment of Imperial General Headquarters, and consular reports on troop movements and public morale during the Second Sino-Japanese War. The second part (pages 9–14) registers reports compiled by the War Department's Military Intelligence Division (MID) and U.S. military attachés, detailing Japanese combat estimates, wartime economic mobilization, defense budgets, field operations in China, and numerous 'Who's Who in the Army' biographical studies of senior Japanese commanders.",
