   "start_page": 1,
   "summary": "This eight-page cumulative docket list (Sheets 14 through 22 of File 894.20) records State Department despatches, telegrams, and cross-reference sheets concerning Japanese military matters between August 1935 and November 1940. It indexes documentation on pivotal domestic events such as the assassination of Major General Tetsuzan Nagata, the subsequent court-martial of Saburo Aizawa, and the February 26, 1936 military coup d'état attempt. In addition, it tracks the passage and implementation of the National General Mobilization Law, the establishment of Imperial General Headquarters, and regular consular reporting from Kobe on embarkations, casualties, and local public sentiment during the Second Sino-Japanese War.",
